WEBVTT

00:11.644 --> 00:16.144
<i>Heavy stones of fate
are holding down my dreams</i>

00:16.982 --> 00:20.443
<i>It feels as if I'm being crushed</i>

00:22.238 --> 00:26.738
<i>I've been staggering around
with nowhere to hide</i>

00:27.409 --> 00:31.246
<i>But I will never give in</i>

00:31.288 --> 00:35.788
<i>I know there are fragments of hope
buried beneath all that rubble</i>

00:43.092 --> 00:47.592
<i>I will find them with my own hands
and turn this world upside down</i>

00:56.146 --> 01:00.646
<i>Fighting gold
We will shine one day</i>

01:02.111 --> 01:06.611
<i>As long as we continue to
believe in our own path</i>

01:09.201 --> 01:12.329
<i>We are unyielding souls</i>

01:12.413 --> 01:16.913
<i>Our battle against god
will keep raging on</i>

01:17.626 --> 01:22.126
<i>Until our final days
Fighting gold</i>

01:31.890 --> 01:36.390
EPISODE 21
THE MYSTERY OF EMPEROR CRIMSON

01:32.808 --> 01:34.392
Hey, Narancia!

01:34.435 --> 01:36.750
Ever heard of helping
your teammates out and sharing?

01:37.813 --> 01:39.981
Give 'em back!
I bought those with…

01:40.024 --> 01:42.943
- my own damn money, you bastard!
- Narancia, you little…

01:42.985 --> 01:44.987
- There are only three left!
- Greedy bastardo.

01:45.029 --> 01:47.031
You'd have to be a complete idiot to
not know we're all starving!

01:47.990 --> 01:51.159
It's on the move again.
It's descending from the top of the tower.

01:51.201 --> 01:51.993
I can feel it.

01:52.411 --> 01:54.079
He's heading down to the crypt…

01:54.163 --> 01:55.706
He's trying to cut through
to the other side.

01:56.165 --> 01:59.626
Bucciarati must've fastened
the brooch to the Boss's clothes.

02:00.002 --> 02:03.714
Sorry, Giorno,
could you pass me the water?

02:04.131 --> 02:05.257
I'm feeling a little parched.

02:05.883 --> 02:08.594
And don't forget,
we have to watch ourselves.

02:08.761 --> 02:13.140
We can't set foot on the island.
We have to stay put.

02:13.182 --> 02:15.225
Those were our orders.

02:15.225 --> 02:15.934
Right.

02:20.022 --> 02:21.690
Huh? Eh?

02:21.690 --> 02:24.401
Couldn't help yourself, huh, Mista?!

02:24.401 --> 02:27.529
Give them back, damn it!

02:27.738 --> 02:30.031
And what the hell is that
on your face?

02:30.032 --> 02:30.574
Huh?

02:31.241 --> 02:31.908
Ah!

02:32.242 --> 02:34.577
Nice try, loser…
You couldn't fool me in a million years!

02:34.620 --> 02:37.497
- When did you cram them in your mouth?
- They're amazing!

02:40.084 --> 02:42.294
Yeah, and did I already
thank you, Giorno?

02:42.711 --> 02:45.130
I don't think I did…
You know, for the water.

02:54.556 --> 02:56.724
<i>This is… bizarre…</i>

03:05.734 --> 03:08.027
I don't know what's going on…

03:08.487 --> 03:09.946
I've got this weird chill.

03:11.198 --> 03:12.449
Hey, coglione!

03:12.491 --> 03:15.744
What about don't disembark
do you not—?

03:16.787 --> 03:17.454
What?

03:17.830 --> 03:18.455
Huh?!

03:19.915 --> 03:21.291
We're in deep trouble.

03:21.917 --> 03:24.461
The world isn't working
the way it's supposed to!

03:24.712 --> 03:26.338
Merda! Bucciarati!

03:26.422 --> 03:28.424
What the hell, Giorno?!

03:28.966 --> 03:29.800
<i>Is that you, Giorno?</i>

03:29.883 --> 03:30.800
Bucciarati!

03:31.343 --> 03:34.137
Yes, and I am tracking him now.

03:34.221 --> 03:37.766
The brooch tells me
his exact location at all times.

03:37.766 --> 03:40.810
He's at the bottom of the stairs
to the crypt right now.

03:40.853 --> 03:43.355
He's by the pillar,
two meters from the stairs.

03:44.440 --> 03:46.150
But wait, Bucciarati!

03:46.191 --> 03:48.985
Something is wrong!

03:50.612 --> 03:55.112
Bucciarati, your mission as protector

03:55.576 --> 03:57.828
has come to an end.

04:06.879 --> 04:08.297
Cunning little…

04:08.589 --> 04:11.049
<i>You're trying top in down my arm.</i>

04:11.091 --> 04:13.051
Zipper Man!

04:13.093 --> 04:17.013
But… Emperor Crimson knows all…

04:31.487 --> 04:32.529
He peered into another time.

04:33.322 --> 04:35.240
To trace your trajectory.

04:35.324 --> 04:37.576
The trajectory of your future self.

04:38.202 --> 04:42.702
When Emperor Crimson wields its power,

04:42.998 --> 04:45.250
time as we know it flits away,

04:45.334 --> 04:48.545
and all memories formed therein
cease to exist.

04:49.671 --> 04:52.757
The billowing clouds above
are torn asunder and know not why.

04:53.008 --> 04:56.011
The flickering flame is blotted
into nothingness

04:56.053 --> 04:57.888
without any consciousness of its demise.

04:58.305 --> 05:00.849
All that remains are
the consequences of its power.

05:01.099 --> 05:04.352
The omnipotence of
my time-obliterating powers

05:04.394 --> 05:06.020
renders all action futile!

05:06.438 --> 05:10.150
Only I can respond to these actions
veiled in temporal mystery.

05:10.192 --> 05:13.320
I can foretell the exact flavor
of your intentions!

05:13.362 --> 05:16.698
Feel the power of Emperor Crimson!

05:33.215 --> 05:36.426
Th-This ability…

05:36.468 --> 05:38.595
No being is immune.

05:38.637 --> 05:42.474
Life abounds with peaks and valleys.

05:42.558 --> 05:45.185
One succeeds and one fails.

05:45.686 --> 05:50.186
But when you gaze upon life's pitfalls
in all its imminent glory,

05:52.234 --> 05:54.486
you can sidestep
what was once inevitable.

05:54.528 --> 05:57.447
Life becomes a succession of triumphs.

05:59.324 --> 06:01.784
You live in a state of personal perfection.

06:02.202 --> 06:03.870
How could you not?

06:09.459 --> 06:11.961
Meeting you in the flesh,

06:12.045 --> 06:16.424
I know now we are
connected by blood.

06:17.092 --> 06:21.592
I can feel it in my bones.
Without a doubt you are my daughter.

06:22.973 --> 06:25.475
Which means…

06:25.809 --> 06:27.852
for as long as you are conscious,

06:27.936 --> 06:31.356
you too will feel the bloodline
that connects us!

06:32.649 --> 06:33.941
Trish…

06:33.942 --> 06:37.820
I will obliterate any peril
that stands in my way!

06:38.113 --> 06:41.658
I will sever our familial bond of blood!

06:41.658 --> 06:42.950
Trish!

06:47.372 --> 06:49.624
W-What?!

06:54.713 --> 06:55.714
That's Giorno…

06:56.632 --> 06:59.968
That's the power of Golden Wind…

07:00.510 --> 07:02.845
<i>He implanted the brooch with
cells from the turtle,</i>

07:02.930 --> 07:04.890
<i>turning the inanimate
into the animate.</i>

07:05.474 --> 07:08.602
<i>That's how he was able to
replicate the turtle's Stand.</i>

07:08.936 --> 07:10.979
<i>Communication was interrupted…</i>

07:11.021 --> 07:13.565
<i>He sensed danger,
and activated his ability</i>

07:14.816 --> 07:18.194
<i>He never ceases
to fill me with courage…</i>

07:19.321 --> 07:22.866
<i>I was certain this was the end,
but… not yet.</i>

07:24.242 --> 07:25.201
<i>I still…</i>

07:26.286 --> 07:28.788
<i>have a little left to give.</i>

07:29.539 --> 07:33.543
So you think my mission is done…?
You're dead wrong, Boss.

07:34.044 --> 07:35.503
Our future awaits!

07:36.129 --> 07:37.338
As for Trish…

07:37.798 --> 07:40.550
she will be protected
under my mandate now!

07:40.842 --> 07:44.387
<i>So he can anticipate any attack,</i>

07:44.429 --> 07:48.683
<i>leaving his victims
completely unaware of what transpired,</i>

07:49.726 --> 07:53.062
<i>and granting him invincibility
and utter transcendence.</i>

07:56.066 --> 07:57.484
Or so it appears…

07:59.736 --> 08:01.237
He's powerful all right…

08:01.279 --> 08:04.448
But he can read his opponent's
movements for only so long!

08:05.200 --> 08:06.951
<i>I'd call it ephemeral.</i>

08:07.369 --> 08:10.413
<i>He can cheat time and peek into
the future for five, maybe ten seconds.</i>

08:11.123 --> 08:12.290
<i>Distance…</i>

08:12.374 --> 08:14.751
<i>I need to create more distance
between the two of us now!</i>

08:15.669 --> 08:18.421
<i>Far enough so that the Boss
can't get a hold of Trish!</i>

08:20.424 --> 08:22.801
<i>Come on, Bruno, move.</i>

08:23.677 --> 08:26.221
<i>Giorno has handed you
an opportunity to act!</i>

08:27.180 --> 08:30.099
<i>Until I can get out of this basement…</i>

08:30.100 --> 08:33.394
So another traitor
has graced us with his presence.

08:34.312 --> 08:35.646
Must be the neophyte.

08:36.023 --> 08:40.523
Assuming my sources are correct,
his name is Giorno Giovanna.

08:41.403 --> 08:45.615
So he had every intention of betraying me
from the very beginning.

08:46.199 --> 08:48.117
How charming that
you think you can escape

08:48.201 --> 08:49.827
by simply moving
farther away from me.

08:49.911 --> 08:53.331
I can just exit this turtle
a moment before you act.

08:53.832 --> 08:57.293
You are utterly pathetic, Bucciarati.

08:58.420 --> 09:00.547
Is it inner strength?

09:00.589 --> 09:01.965
Is that why you can move?

09:02.340 --> 09:04.467
Why not simply lay
your head down to rest?

09:04.509 --> 09:06.511
You may never reach the first floor,

09:06.553 --> 09:08.930
but you will be assured
a painless passage to the other side.

09:09.765 --> 09:12.559
Now to eliminate Trish.

09:12.934 --> 09:15.686
Remain still, Bucciarati!

09:15.771 --> 09:18.982
Giorno gave me a chance,
and I didn't waste it!

09:19.066 --> 09:21.318
While you were bragging about
reading my movements,

09:21.359 --> 09:23.277
I took the liberty of reading yours!

09:23.862 --> 09:26.155
I knew you wouldn't
fall into the sewer before

09:26.198 --> 09:29.117
trying to escape using your powers!

09:29.117 --> 09:32.161
Now, Zipper Man!

09:33.371 --> 09:34.830
Emperor Crimson!

09:45.467 --> 09:46.759
That was close…

09:47.552 --> 09:50.846
But in the world of Emperor Crimson,

09:51.223 --> 09:54.184
your efforts are forever in vain!

09:54.559 --> 09:55.393
Perish!

09:55.811 --> 09:57.062
This is the end!

09:57.896 --> 10:00.189
I wasn't aiming for you.

10:00.232 --> 10:01.858
It was this pillar!

10:01.900 --> 10:04.027
Zipper, close!

10:05.737 --> 10:06.738
What?!

10:06.822 --> 10:07.697
I was right…

10:07.739 --> 10:10.575
Your power is
overwhelmingly formidable…

10:10.700 --> 10:15.200
But your ability to foretell
my movements is extremely limited.

10:15.247 --> 10:18.375
You're not really peering into the future.

10:19.459 --> 10:23.337
I challenge you to predict
what I will do next, Boss.

10:23.839 --> 10:27.384
Who knows what the next few seconds
in the future may hold?

10:27.968 --> 10:30.303
I invite you to face your future.

10:30.762 --> 10:33.347
You will be greeted by the sight of me

10:33.682 --> 10:35.183
standing firmly on the first floor.

10:46.778 --> 10:48.571
Bucciarati! Trish!

10:51.908 --> 10:52.992
This wound…

10:53.326 --> 10:54.827
What happened in the crypt?!

10:57.372 --> 10:58.289
Where's the Boss?

11:01.209 --> 11:02.418
<i>He's got to be here…</i>

11:02.878 --> 11:04.588
<i>He's somewhere close by</i>

11:05.505 --> 11:09.008
<i>I don't know what happened,
but I know one thing…</i>

11:09.176 --> 11:11.386
<i>The Boss doesn't tolerate
any act of defiance,</i>

11:11.428 --> 11:12.637
<i>and that includes Bucciarati!</i>

11:20.478 --> 11:21.520
Bucciarati…

11:24.357 --> 11:25.441
N-No…

11:25.859 --> 11:26.776
Bucciarati!

11:34.242 --> 11:35.368
It's gone…

11:35.619 --> 11:37.579
He… He has no pulse!

11:38.163 --> 11:41.124
I made the replacement part…
He should be breathing!

11:41.166 --> 11:43.084
Come on, Bucciarati, breathe!

11:43.752 --> 11:45.879
<i>So this is the Giorno Giovanna.</i>

11:46.713 --> 11:51.213
<i>His peculiar powers gave Bucciarati
another chance at life.</i>

11:52.594 --> 11:53.386
<i>Interesting…</i>

11:54.262 --> 11:56.180
<i>Sad, such a valiant effort!</i>

11:56.640 --> 11:57.932
This is impossible!

11:58.391 --> 11:59.892
He should be fine with the replacement!

12:00.602 --> 12:02.562
It makes no sense
that he'd have no pulse!

12:02.604 --> 12:04.355
<i>Giorno, it's me.</i>

12:05.190 --> 12:06.733
<i>Call Abbacchio and the others.</i>

12:07.150 --> 12:08.317
<i>You have to escape.</i>

12:11.446 --> 12:12.738
That voice…

12:13.240 --> 12:16.201
I told you to call
Abbacchio and the others.

12:16.826 --> 12:18.035
Get out of here!

12:18.578 --> 12:19.870
Leave the basilica!

12:20.580 --> 12:21.330
Do it now!

12:21.331 --> 12:22.832
B-Bucciarati!

12:23.124 --> 12:24.208
Th-Thank god!

12:24.668 --> 12:25.669
You're really okay!

12:25.669 --> 12:28.171
Quickly, call the others now!

12:28.171 --> 12:29.839
B-But…

12:29.839 --> 12:33.342
The Boss's identity will have to
remain a mystery for now.

12:33.343 --> 12:36.012
We need to get out of here, Giorno!
Our lead won't last long!

12:36.096 --> 12:37.806
<i>You're within range!</i>

12:37.806 --> 12:38.640
<i>Let's begin!</i>

12:39.975 --> 12:43.561
I'll explain later! Hurry up, Giorno!

12:44.729 --> 12:46.731
Golden Wind!

12:52.153 --> 12:53.696
Giorno's over there!

12:54.739 --> 12:57.533
Hey, Giorno, you bastard!
Get your ass back here!

12:57.659 --> 12:59.535
How do you think the Boss
is gonna react

12:59.619 --> 13:01.078
when he finds out you refused
to stay in the boat?!

13:01.162 --> 13:02.788
Bucciarati's here, too!

13:02.998 --> 13:05.291
What happened, you look awful?!

13:05.333 --> 13:07.376
And why is Trish in your arms?!

13:07.669 --> 13:09.837
What's going on here, Bucciarati?

13:09.838 --> 13:11.089
I'll explain everything later.

13:11.172 --> 13:13.048
What matters now is that
we get out of this building.

13:13.383 --> 13:15.551
<i>Bucciarati, I salute you.</i>

13:16.303 --> 13:19.639
<i>You are a man
of unerring judgment.</i>

13:19.681 --> 13:22.517
<i>I may have the power to
obliterate time at my finger tips,</i>

13:22.767 --> 13:27.267
<i>but facing six Stand users now
will inevitably reveal my identity</i>

13:32.777 --> 13:34.403
<i>Now is not the time…</i>

13:34.821 --> 13:37.990
<i>You were fortunate to survive
Emperor Crimson for now.</i>

13:38.491 --> 13:41.744
<i>But I can assure you
your fortuitousness will be short-lived</i>

13:42.203 --> 13:43.287
<i>I promise you…</i>

13:43.705 --> 13:45.581
<i>you shall die here…</i>

13:45.582 --> 13:47.500
<i>Venezia will be your watery grave!</i>

13:48.543 --> 13:50.086
I figured it out…

13:50.128 --> 13:54.628
I know now how he foments fear
and clings to power.

13:55.383 --> 13:57.760
We can't defeat the Boss…
Not now.

13:58.636 --> 14:00.179
His identity…

14:00.221 --> 14:02.765
Assuming he has any weakness,

14:03.099 --> 14:06.185
we'll need to decipher his flaws
before we can even think of taking him on!

14:11.524 --> 14:13.442
EMPEROR CRIMSON

14:14.819 --> 14:15.820
What…?

14:16.196 --> 14:18.114
What the hell's going on, Bucciarati?

14:18.531 --> 14:19.907
You better start talking.

14:19.949 --> 14:21.784
What's gotten into you?

14:23.870 --> 14:26.289
I hear you.
I'll cut right to the chase.

14:28.458 --> 14:30.293
I can't go into detail right now.

14:30.377 --> 14:33.463
I don't have to tell you
we are in serious danger.

14:35.090 --> 14:37.884
I brought Trish back to us here…

14:38.426 --> 14:40.469
because I've committed to
betraying the Boss.

14:41.846 --> 14:43.639
Well, men, I suppose
this is where I say goodbye.

14:44.265 --> 14:48.765
If you choose to join me,
you too will become a traitor.

14:50.021 --> 14:51.689
W-What?

14:51.773 --> 14:54.066
I-I'm not processing…

14:54.109 --> 14:56.361
W-What did you just say?

14:56.403 --> 15:00.156
He said…
he betrayed the Boss.

15:00.448 --> 15:01.824
B-But why?

15:02.784 --> 15:05.536
I think it's best
we end this conversation here.

15:06.287 --> 15:08.789
This is a choice I have chosen to make.

15:09.749 --> 15:11.667
No, I think you should elaborate.

15:12.210 --> 15:15.004
Some of us may want to join you.

15:15.547 --> 15:17.882
Besides… you need allies.

15:18.967 --> 15:22.637
You know, Giorno,
you really are a piece of work!

15:22.637 --> 15:25.723
First, you march into the basilica
like you own the place, and now—

15:27.016 --> 15:28.058
Bucciarati!

15:28.726 --> 15:30.853
What's wrong?
Are you all right?

15:30.854 --> 15:32.188
I'm fine.

15:32.856 --> 15:36.192
The loss of blood made me a little dizzy.

15:36.943 --> 15:38.527
<i>It doesn't make sense…</i>

15:38.903 --> 15:41.697
<i>I replaced the wound with healthy tissue
and replenished his blood too.</i>

15:42.323 --> 15:44.074
<i>Did I miss something?</i>

15:47.454 --> 15:49.873
The whole ordeal
has fatigued me, that's all.

15:49.914 --> 15:53.876
<i>He didn't feel that?
He's not bleeding a tall.</i>

15:54.335 --> 15:55.294
<i>My eyes playing tricks on me?</i>

15:55.336 --> 15:56.545
You'll have to excuse me.

15:56.629 --> 15:58.380
You really scared me there!

15:58.465 --> 15:59.757
For Christ sake.

15:59.841 --> 16:01.717
Bucciarati, please…

16:02.177 --> 16:03.720
Yeah, Bucciarati.

16:04.220 --> 16:06.055
You have a lot to catch us up on.

16:15.356 --> 16:17.066
The Boss only had us
protect his daughter

16:17.108 --> 16:21.608
so that he could be assured
he could kill her himself.

16:22.238 --> 16:23.656
They share the same bloodline,

16:23.698 --> 16:25.866
which means she has insight
into the Boss's identity.

16:26.159 --> 16:28.244
Once I learned the truth, I…

16:29.037 --> 16:30.997
I knew I could never forgive him.

16:31.247 --> 16:32.706
I couldn't stand before you here

16:32.749 --> 16:35.084
and ignore the evil that
was just seared into my memory.

16:35.877 --> 16:37.336
I had to betray him!

16:38.046 --> 16:39.380
I'm at a loss…

16:39.422 --> 16:41.715
Are you nuts, Bucciarati?

16:42.175 --> 16:45.052
I know I don't have to tell you
what happens to traitors of the famiglia…

16:45.094 --> 16:47.096
He makes no exceptions.

16:47.180 --> 16:50.349
He will punish the perpetrator!

16:50.391 --> 16:54.891
Heck, I bet he and his bodyguards
already have this place on lockdown!

16:55.146 --> 16:58.482
Yes, that's why I'll need your help.

16:59.150 --> 17:01.193
If you choose to join me
in this operation,

17:01.903 --> 17:04.447
then descend these stairs
and board this vessel.

17:05.198 --> 17:09.160
Let me be clear that this is
not an order, but an invitation.

17:09.911 --> 17:12.246
The decision is entirely yours,
and yours alone, to make.

17:12.830 --> 17:14.957
I am under no illusion that
this decision isn't entirely mine.

17:14.999 --> 17:17.918
You have no duty or obligation
to follow me.

17:17.919 --> 17:21.339
You may think me conceited,
but say it I must.

17:21.923 --> 17:24.342
I know my actions are just and good.

17:25.009 --> 17:25.968
I have no regrets.

17:26.469 --> 17:30.969
Our world may be unjust,
but I refuse to live someone else's life.

17:31.766 --> 17:33.434
Once we find his weakness…

17:33.768 --> 17:35.436
our retreat now doesn't matter.

17:35.478 --> 17:37.480
I will destroy the Boss.

17:37.981 --> 17:39.941
I will pinpoint his Achilles' heel!

18:00.128 --> 18:01.671
Everything makes sense.

18:01.713 --> 18:04.674
I really do get it…
Your actions are just, Bucciarati.

18:05.216 --> 18:07.676
But I have to speak my truth too…

18:08.469 --> 18:11.763
It hurts to say this,
but no one is going to step onto that boat.

18:12.515 --> 18:15.184
Frankly, I'm surprised you're being
so sentimental about all this.

18:15.810 --> 18:19.188
I owe you my life,
but I can't be a part of this.

18:19.814 --> 18:21.690
You've lost touch with reality.

18:22.108 --> 18:25.361
Lofty ideals alone won't get you through
the really hard times in this life.

18:25.903 --> 18:28.530
We can't make it through
without the famiglia.

18:29.073 --> 18:30.866
What Fugo's saying is right.

18:31.159 --> 18:34.203
You might as well have committed suicide.

18:34.203 --> 18:36.246
There's nowhere you can hide now,

18:36.289 --> 18:38.833
you'll have to live life
always on the run.

18:39.125 --> 18:42.378
Remember, I pledged my allegiance
to the famiglia at large.

18:43.004 --> 18:45.715
Never did my loyalty lie with you.

18:48.676 --> 18:49.927
Even so…

18:51.095 --> 18:55.595
I've never had a place to really call home,
a place where I felt I really belonged.

18:57.185 --> 18:59.729
The only time I've ever been
able to feel at ease

19:00.146 --> 19:03.440
is working with you, Bucciarati.

19:05.860 --> 19:06.861
Abbacchio…

19:08.529 --> 19:11.281
Listen to yourself, Abbacchio!

19:11.532 --> 19:14.117
Well, if we get rid of the Boss…

19:14.285 --> 19:16.245
Considering my skills…

19:16.621 --> 19:18.623
the next one to be capo is moi.

19:19.582 --> 19:22.126
Listen, Bucciarati is one smart stronzo.

19:22.168 --> 19:25.254
He'd never take on
an opponent he couldn't beat.

19:25.338 --> 19:28.090
We're gonna be rolling in
all that sweet, sweet lira.

19:28.841 --> 19:30.717
Mista! Not you, too!

19:31.219 --> 19:34.138
What is your plan, Fugo?

19:34.681 --> 19:37.517
You've all completely lost it!

19:37.558 --> 19:39.393
We'll be completely isolated!

19:39.394 --> 19:41.437
Where the hell
do you think you can run?

19:41.521 --> 19:44.732
It's… It's not like you could
make it out of this city alive!

19:44.732 --> 19:45.899
Narancia…

19:46.234 --> 19:47.902
What are you going to do?

19:48.361 --> 19:51.739
I-I d-don't know…

19:52.281 --> 19:54.032
Tell me, Bucciarati…

19:54.283 --> 19:56.827
What should I do?

19:56.911 --> 19:58.704
Do you think I should go?

19:59.080 --> 19:59.955
You're scared?

20:00.164 --> 20:03.125
Yeah… I'm r-really scared…

20:03.167 --> 20:05.502
Just give me an order!

20:05.586 --> 20:08.964
Just tell me to get my ass in gear
like you always do!

20:09.048 --> 20:12.092
Give me an order,
and I won't be afraid anymore!

20:12.093 --> 20:13.135
I won't.

20:13.636 --> 20:15.471
This is one thing
I can't order you to do.

20:15.513 --> 20:16.931
You have to make your own choice.

20:17.140 --> 20:21.060
Your path in life is yours to decide.

20:21.269 --> 20:25.769
B-But I don't know!
I don't know!

20:26.274 --> 20:28.276
A word of caution.

20:29.068 --> 20:30.652
Don't join me, Narancia.

20:31.320 --> 20:32.988
This is not your fight.

20:37.118 --> 20:38.327
You really are serious?

20:38.661 --> 20:40.412
You'll end up six feet under.

20:40.496 --> 20:43.123
Some things in this world
you just can't change,

20:43.166 --> 20:44.500
even with the best intentions.

20:44.876 --> 20:48.212
We as mafiosi can't always
take the moral high ground.

20:48.254 --> 20:51.257
How is the predicament we're facing now
any different from all the other times?

20:51.799 --> 20:52.966
This is different…

20:53.009 --> 20:55.344
I refuse to live a life of
lies and delusions.

20:58.473 --> 20:59.474
Let's go!

20:59.515 --> 21:03.060
Our departure will mark
the beginning of your lives as traitors!

21:07.482 --> 21:10.151
Come on, guys…
Think about this!

21:10.151 --> 21:11.402
We just met this girl.

21:11.486 --> 21:14.614
We know absolutely
nothing about her!

21:14.655 --> 21:17.616
She won't even tell us
what kind of music she likes!

21:23.372 --> 21:26.625
Trish was rejected by the one person
she thought she could trust…

21:28.920 --> 21:32.006
I know how she feels…
I know the pain of rejection.

21:32.465 --> 21:33.924
My own father…

21:34.050 --> 21:37.511
The people I thought were my friends…
They all gave up on me.

21:38.179 --> 21:40.222
- We're the same…
- The Boss's actions may be horrible,

21:40.264 --> 21:41.890
- We share a lot…
- but it has nothing to do with us!

21:42.433 --> 21:44.101
- Trish and I are a lot alike!
- None of this has to be this way…

21:44.101 --> 21:46.228
- Trish and I are a lot alike!
- None of this makes any sense!

21:49.023 --> 21:51.066
Giorno, the turtle please.

21:52.026 --> 21:53.777
Trish can hide inside.

21:53.861 --> 21:54.695
Okay.

21:56.531 --> 21:59.075
Bucciarati, you should turn around.

21:59.075 --> 22:02.244
Bucciarati!

22:03.704 --> 22:07.582
I'll go! I'm right behind you…
Don't leave me!

22:08.084 --> 22:11.003
Please, please don't tell me
to stay behind!

22:11.045 --> 22:15.545
Trish is me! She's me…
Her wounds are my wounds!

22:20.263 --> 22:22.682
Narancia… Not you, too…

22:23.474 --> 22:26.268
Idiota… You're going to be killed.

22:30.189 --> 22:33.609
I can't be a part of
this foolish game of betrayal.

22:34.318 --> 22:36.945
I refuse to become a virtuous victim…

22:42.827 --> 22:45.496
You sure took your sweet ass time.

22:45.580 --> 22:48.541
You'd better not bitch about this
to us later on, ya got it?

22:48.916 --> 22:52.169
Narancia, that was an act of courage,
and you have my complete respect.

22:53.296 --> 22:55.798
So that bastard Fugo ditched us.

22:56.215 --> 22:59.176
The decision was his alone to make.

23:03.222 --> 23:04.139
Bucciarati!

23:04.473 --> 23:07.184
I… I want to protect Trish!

23:07.852 --> 23:09.603
I'll defeat the Boss with you!

23:10.479 --> 23:11.396
Yeah.

23:20.114 --> 23:21.573
Squalo?

23:21.616 --> 23:25.453
We have ourselves some traitors…
In Venezia.

23:25.494 --> 23:29.790
Their names are Bruno Bucciarati
and Giorno Giovanna.

23:29.665 --> 23:34.165
BOSS'S IDENTITY: UNKNOWN
STAND NAME: EMPEROR CRIMSON
POWER… OBLITERATING TIME,
PREDICTING THE FUTURE,
INVINCIBILITY.

23:30.416 --> 23:33.043
Capture them dead or alive.

23:33.085 --> 23:34.232
Boss's direct orders!

23:38.591 --> 23:41.927
EPISODE 22
THE "G" IN GOZZO
